% ============================================================================
% reaction-types.query.adj — a worked recall over the chemistry reaction-types
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how do you classify a
% combustion reaction?": it states no chemistry fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves
% each `?` against the `reaction_defining` rows and returns the defining token +
% the table's source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD
% (bind the defining token `breaks_down`, recall its type — decomposition). A
% word that is not one of the five basic reaction types abstains honestly — the
% engine never invents a definition.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli reaction-types.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "reaction-types.adj"

? reaction_defining(combination, $Defining)     % expect two_or_more_combine
? reaction_defining(combustion, $Defining)      % expect reacts_with_oxygen
? reaction_defining(double_replacement, $Defining) % expect ions_exchange_places
? reaction_defining($Type, breaks_down)         % reverse bind — expect decomposition
? reaction_defining(neutralization, $Defining)  % expect abstain — neutralization is not one of the five basic reaction types
